				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify the Ubuntu operating system enforces a delay of at least 4 seconds between logon prompts following a failed logon attempt with the following command: 
 
$ grep pam_faildelay /etc/pam.d/common-auth 
 
auth    required    pam_faildelay.so    delay=4000000 
 
If the line is not present or is commented out, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure the Ubuntu operating system to enforce a delay of at least 4 seconds between logon prompts following a failed logon attempt. 
 
Edit the file "/etc/pam.d/common-auth" and set the parameter "pam_faildelay" to a value of  4000000 or greater: 
 
auth    required    pam_faildelay.so    delay=4000000</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
