					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify the Ubuntu operating system generates an audit record upon successful/unsuccessful modifications to the "tallylog" file. 
 
Check the currently configured audit rules with the following command: 
 
$ sudo auditctl -l | grep tallylog 
 
-w /var/log/tallylog -p wa -k logins 
 
If the command does not return a line that matches the example or the line is commented out, this is a finding. 
 
Note: The "-k" allows for specifying an arbitrary identifier, and the string after it does not need to match the example output above.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
